<Project>
  <!--
    ShadowStrike solution-wide MSBuild defaults.

    Pin the 64-bit hosted MSVC toolchain for every C++ project.

    Rationale: PhantomEmulator/Core/JIT/JITCompiler.cpp defines JITCompiler::Impl,
    which embeds std::array<RuntimeBlock, kMaxCompiledBlocks> runtimeBlocks{} where
    each RuntimeBlock itself contains a large std::array<DecodedInstruction, ...>.
    Value-initializing that deeply-nested, multi-megabyte aggregate under /O2 makes
    the optimizer's working set exceed the ~3-4 GB address space of the 32-bit
    hosted cl.exe, which then aborts with:
        fatal error C1060: compiler is out of heap space
    The 64-bit hosted compiler (HostX64) has no such address-space ceiling and
    compiles the translation unit cleanly. PreferredToolArchitecture=x64 selects it.
    This is the Microsoft-recommended remedy for C1060 and does not alter codegen.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PreferredToolArchitecture>x64</PreferredToolArchitecture>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
